{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-37067" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the vertical asymptotes of $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}-4}{2{x}^{2}+5x+2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063519/state.json" "file_sha256" "625df3e3bb64b18b1721f21af53d0cca2b5f49e51c48223accb4f12539686638"} {"question" "q-37067" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We start by factoring the function as much as possible and canceling the common factors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}-4}{2{x}^{2}+5x+2} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}-{2}^{2}}{2{x}^{2}+4x+x+2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+2)(x-2)}{2x(x+2)+(x+2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+2)(x-2)}{(2x+1)(x+2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{(x+2)}(x-2)}{(2x+1)\\cancel{(x+2)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{x-2}{2x+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now set the denominator equal to zero:\n\n$$\n2x+1=0\\,⟹\\,x=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the *only* vertical asymptote is at $x=-\\frac{1}{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063519/state.json" "file_sha256" "625df3e3bb64b18b1721f21af53d0cca2b5f49e51c48223accb4f12539686638"} {"question" "q-37067" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063519/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a1fe7ff3b1b70ad97b954e0de6b237dcfef21b27e0e424dc3281303107715c10"} {"question" "q-37067" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063519/state.json" "file_sha256" "625df3e3bb64b18b1721f21af53d0cca2b5f49e51c48223accb4f12539686638"} {"question" "q-37067" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=-2"] ["math" "x=-\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "x=\\frac{4}{3}"] ["text" "$x=-\\frac{1}{2}$, $x=-2$"] ["text" "No vertical  asymptotes"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063519/state.json" "file_sha256" "625df3e3bb64b18b1721f21af53d0cca2b5f49e51c48223accb4f12539686638"} {"question" "q-37067" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=-\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063519/state.json" "file_sha256" "625df3e3bb64b18b1721f21af53d0cca2b5f49e51c48223accb4f12539686638"} {"question" "q-73015" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the vertical asymptotes of $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}}{2x+4}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063519/state.json" "file_sha256" "625df3e3bb64b18b1721f21af53d0cca2b5f49e51c48223accb4f12539686638"} {"question" "q-73015" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's simplify the expression by factoring both the numerator and the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}}{2x+4} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}(x+2)}{2(x+2)}=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the denominator is never zero, we conclude that this function has no vertical asymptotes. A plot of the function is below. Note that it is not defined at $x=-2.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063519/assets/3ad83a79ccd47d9d035ac5a3f47b929a1e6b3939cdaddee9ff0f2d6a3cf07e56.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063519/state.json" "file_sha256" "625df3e3bb64b18b1721f21af53d0cca2b5f49e51c48223accb4f12539686638"} {"question" "q-73015" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063519/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a1fe7ff3b1b70ad97b954e0de6b237dcfef21b27e0e424dc3281303107715c10"} {"question" "q-73015" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063519/state.json" "file_sha256" "625df3e3bb64b18b1721f21af53d0cca2b5f49e51c48223accb4f12539686638"} {"question" "q-73015" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=-10"] ["math" "x=-2"] ["math" "x=2"] ["text" "$x=0$, $x=-2$"] ["text" "No vertical asymptotes"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063519/state.json" "file_sha256" "625df3e3bb64b18b1721f21af53d0cca2b5f49e51c48223accb4f12539686638"} {"question" "q-73015" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "No vertical asymptotes"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063519/state.json" "file_sha256" "625df3e3bb64b18b1721f21af53d0cca2b5f49e51c48223accb4f12539686638"} {"question" "q-107038" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the vertical asymptotes of $f(x)=\\frac{(x+2)({x}^{4}+{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2})}{{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063519/state.json" "file_sha256" "625df3e3bb64b18b1721f21af53d0cca2b5f49e51c48223accb4f12539686638"} {"question" "q-107038" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's simplify the expression by factoring both the numerator and the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x+2)({x}^{4}+{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2})}{{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}(x+2)({x}^{2}+x-6)}{{x}^{2}(x+2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{{x}^{2}(x+2)}({x}^{2}+x-6)}{\\cancel{{x}^{2}(x+2)}} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+x-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the denominator is never zero, we conclude that this function has no vertical asymptotes. A plot of the function is below. Note that it is not defined at $x=-2$ and $x=0.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063519/assets/31f16682ad863f5f320130705ac57415a74340f3fe73a67a03b4df258c2577e7.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063519/state.json" "file_sha256" "625df3e3bb64b18b1721f21af53d0cca2b5f49e51c48223accb4f12539686638"} {"question" "q-107038" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063519/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a1fe7ff3b1b70ad97b954e0de6b237dcfef21b27e0e424dc3281303107715c10"} {"question" "q-107038" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063519/state.json" "file_sha256" "625df3e3bb64b18b1721f21af53d0cca2b5f49e51c48223accb4f12539686638"} {"question" "q-107038" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=-2"] ["math" "x=-2,3"] ["math" "x=0"] ["math" "x=2"] ["text" "No vertical asymptotes"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063519/state.json" "file_sha256" "625df3e3bb64b18b1721f21af53d0cca2b5f49e51c48223accb4f12539686638"} {"question" "q-107038" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "No vertical asymptotes"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063519/state.json" "file_sha256" "625df3e3bb64b18b1721f21af53d0cca2b5f49e51c48223accb4f12539686638"} {"question" "q-107075" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the vertical asymptotes of $f(x)=\\frac{5}{2x}+\\frac{3}{4x}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063519/state.json" "file_sha256" "625df3e3bb64b18b1721f21af53d0cca2b5f49e51c48223accb4f12539686638"} {"question" "q-107075" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's put the two terms over a common denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{2x}+\\frac{3}{4x} & =\\frac{5(2)+3}{4x}=\\frac{13}{4x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere are no common factors in the numerator and denominator, so we proceed to set the denominator equal to zero and get\n\n$$\n4x=0\\,⟹\\,x=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertical asymptotes are at $x=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063519/state.json" "file_sha256" "625df3e3bb64b18b1721f21af53d0cca2b5f49e51c48223accb4f12539686638"} {"question" "q-107075" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063519/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a1fe7ff3b1b70ad97b954e0de6b237dcfef21b27e0e424dc3281303107715c10"} {"question" "q-107075" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063519/state.json" "file_sha256" "625df3e3bb64b18b1721f21af53d0cca2b5f49e51c48223accb4f12539686638"} {"question" "q-107075" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=0"] ["math" "x=1"] ["math" "x=\\frac{1}{2}"] ["text" "$x=0$ and $x=1$"] ["text" "No vertical asymptotes"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063519/state.json" "file_sha256" "625df3e3bb64b18b1721f21af53d0cca2b5f49e51c48223accb4f12539686638"} {"question" "q-107075" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063519/state.json" "file_sha256" "625df3e3bb64b18b1721f21af53d0cca2b5f49e51c48223accb4f12539686638"} {"question" "q-339968" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The vertical asymptote of $f(x)=\\frac{8x-16}{{x}^{2}-6x+8}$ is\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063519/state.json" "file_sha256" "625df3e3bb64b18b1721f21af53d0cca2b5f49e51c48223accb4f12539686638"} {"question" "q-339968" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We start by factoring the function as much as possible and canceling the common factors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8x-16}{{x}^{2}-6x+8} & =\\frac{8(x-2)}{(x-2)(x-4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\cancel{(x-2)}}{\\cancel{(x-2)}(x-4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{x-4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now set the denominator equal to zero:\n\n$$\nx-4=0\\,⟹\\,x=4\n$$\n\nSo the *only* vertical asymptote is at $x=4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063519/state.json" "file_sha256" "625df3e3bb64b18b1721f21af53d0cca2b5f49e51c48223accb4f12539686638"} {"question" "q-339968" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063519/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a1fe7ff3b1b70ad97b954e0de6b237dcfef21b27e0e424dc3281303107715c10"} {"question" "q-339968" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063519/state.json" "file_sha256" "625df3e3bb64b18b1721f21af53d0cca2b5f49e51c48223accb4f12539686638"} {"question" "q-339968" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063519/state.json" "file_sha256" "625df3e3bb64b18b1721f21af53d0cca2b5f49e51c48223accb4f12539686638"}] "usage" {} "basis" 2050 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
